**Job Description**
**Key Accountabilities**
* Build SJ/SMEC’s reputation as a leading consultant with a strong reputation for innovation, technical excellence, quality and project delivery;
* Provide technical risk (and opportunity) governance to both proposals and projects to achieve reliable project performance in terms of sophistication, timeliness and quality (e.g. as Proposal/Project Director);
* Support management to provide technical leadership to employees to ensure cohesion, optimal performance, resourcing, retention and professional development of technical staff;
* Support management to achieve sustainable growth of the business through targeted client relationship management (CRM) and business development (BD) activity.


**Experience**
 Atleast 20\+ years of Professional Industry Experience




* Established international industry profile, recognised as a leader in Ports and Maritime;
* Sought out at industry forums.


**Has The Demonstrated Ability To Consistently**
* Provide key technical expertise across a broad range of high profile projects;
* Manage risk on substantial projects;
* Apply safety in design practices and processes;
* Deliver best client outcomes which have resulted in cost savings;
* Establish and maintain client relationships;
* Bring in new business through business development activities;
* Building technical capability of others;
* Provide expert advice and undertake key high level and complex technical tasks with a high degree of independence across a broad range of medium to large projects;
* Successfully monitor and manage the scope and risk of multiple complex and varying size projects and apply business systems;
* Prepare high level complex technical reports and prepare successful proposals on medium to large projects;
* Utilise excellent time management skills with the ability to efficiently plan workloads and meet deadlines;
* Effectively work across a variety of projects continuously learning and applying new skills and knowledge quickly and efficiently;
* Effectively manage client relationships and expectations
* Provide leadership, supervision and coaching to other staff;
* Effectively engage key stakeholders to result in superior project outcomes which meet or exceed client expectations.


**Skills/Knowledge**
* Demonstrated leadership ability;
* High level technical knowledge;
* Business planning, budgeting and commercial acumen;
* High level consulting and client management skills;
* Proven high level project management skills;
* An understanding of the business / organisation / marketing context of business solutions;
* High level of client service orientation;
* Good national and international industry awareness and market knowledge;
* Excellent interpersonal and communication skills to work effectively within a diverse and multi\-disciplinary environment;
* Skilled in managing a co\-operative and flexible work style to work in a team environment;
* Ability to source and apply new knowledge including industry information and key talent;
* Highly skilled in managing competing priorities and working under pressure;
* Computer literacy with proficiency in a variety of relevant computer programs;
* Sound understanding of SMEC's organisational capability and how to access it;
* Aware of SMEC Business Systems in particular:
* Project Management
* WHS Management
* High level application of CRM principals.


 At Surbana Jurong, we put talent, hard work, teamwork and a fun workplace together to approach problems and solve them creatively and collaboratively. Join us in making a positive impact on the world!




